# with the lamp groups the show process owned recorded, and on the light-language builds the light runner's
# commands (shows/scan_job3.sh, scanlog3.so); each is named from what it did - its colours (the RGB inserts its
# groups lit, or the commands' --red/--green/--blue), on/off toggling (a strobe), in-between levels (a fade),
# lights coming on in turn (a chase), how many lights next to the build's biggest show (wide: 80% or more,
# small: 25% or fewer) - and how long it ran (shows/finalname.py; on Godzilla LE's ten it gives PAD-411's
# kinds). None reaches the game's sound, score, coil, award, clip or event calls (shows/showsafe.py), and none
